t  was it was a certainly a different breed  of people i think that that took those  journeys and it's certainly the ones  that made it  mm-hmm  yeah i looked at the opening scenes of  that first episode they went yeah no  that's  there's no way i would have made it i  would have been maybe that first guy  with the wagon that would have been me  just like what we've gotten i'm gone i'm  sure yeah  [Laughter]  so tell me how this came to be that you  and faith  get to do this together get to go on  this adventure together  wow you know it's  i we did i got a call from taylor  last year sometime last year gosh time  has sort of ran together over the last  two or three years as ever for everybody  but i got a call from taylor first my my  agent um from caa brian laps called me  and said that you know taylor sheridan  wants to call you he's alright if i give  him your number and of course i'm like  of course give taylor my number because  we were big yellowstone fans to start  with from the very first episode that it  came out and so i get a phone call and  it's taylor and he go you know he's said  are you a yellowstone fan do you want to  you know i'd like for you to be in the  show do an episode or something and i  said i'd love to but let's come up with  something that's really cool and  interesting and  if you come up with something cool and  interesting you know like i don't want  to be just a singing cowboy that gets  taken to the train station you know come  up with something cool and interesting  and and of course i'll be interested in  he came back and he came up with these  flashback sort of scenes um  with the original duttons who founded  yellowstone  and i thought that that was very  interesting and very cool and and an  interesting way to introduce me as a  character into that show  um and then he called back again he says  well you're gonna have a wife in this  you know see you think maybe  faith would be interested she did so we  did a few episodes um  and then  i guess  december last year  taylor called and said that you know the  the studio has seen the flashback stuff  and and they're  they want to do a whole series off of  this and are you guys interested and  and i was  certainly interested and then when we  started reading the scripts when he  started sending scripts that he had  written for this show  we were blown away and when faith and i  looked at each other and says you know  we we have to find a way to do this  because  you know whatever our schedule is  whatever  time we have  it's just so well written and so good  um the storytelling is so spectacular  and it's so  engaging and it's so tragic and  heartbreaking yeah and real all at the  same time i mean it's very rare that you  get a chance to do this individually  something this this good and this this  much quality and then super rare as  husband and wife to get to do it  together  yeah i mean if i could just gush about  her for a minute  well i mean she really embodies this  strength right like she's she is that  character she's in that role when you  guys are done filming a day  and you've gone through everything that  you've gone through are you reflecting  and going like whoa like  you really surprised me with that beat  or i'm really impressed with how you did  xyz  sometimes you know sometimes we're just  so exhausted that we just eat and go to  bed and go to sleep  but because it's long hours and  and you know it's hard work and  as you can see i mean as you when you  see it it's not just sort of walking  through scenes there's a lot of physical  stuff that goes on but then there's some  nights when you just magic happens and  you have magical scenes where everything  just flows and you almost forget about  it that's when you when you know you're  having really good scenes is when you do  the scene and you almost forget what you  just did because the scene was so good  and then those are the nights that we'll  sit up for a couple hours and talk about  it and talk about how much fun it is and  how excited we are to be able to do this  and and sort of feed off each other's  energy  yeah one thing that's a really nice  thread between both yellowstone and 1883  is that there are some very talented  musicians putting on some  spectacular acting in both of these  movies but i'm curious if if the role if  the the journey and the the difficulty  that you're imagining being in has  actually inspired any music  you know  i've written stuff along the way i mean  i'm actually working on a new album at  the same time that we're they're we're  filming this but um but i've written  stuff along the way for um in fact um  there's an episode coming up where um  um wade's character is singing to the  cattle so i wrote him a little lullaby  for the cattle for it that you'll hear  him sing later on but yeah i mean  there's all i mean for me i mean i could  walk down the street and there's some  sort of song i did that comes to my head  just and that's all about you know  observing life which is which is what  art's all about  right on well man it's i know there's  going to be another one of those shows  everyone's talking about i mean i think  just living in the world the last couple  years  people have been telling me oh watch  allison when you watch yellowstone and i  think this is going to be the next one  everyone's going to talk about 1883 man  good job  thank you i appreciate it

